  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 + transformer (config_006) achieves 0.653 acc, establishing a strong RNA baseline. Image-only models are very weak (resnet50: 0.208, ViT-L: 0.227), raising the critical question of whether adding image to the dominant RNA signal helps, is neutral, or hurts. No multimodal configuration has been tested yet, so we have zero evidence on fusion utility. This experiment (config_039: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) directly tests whether the image modality provides complementary information to the best RNA configuration. Weighted fusion is chosen over concat because the image signal is ~3x weaker; weighted allows the model to downweight uninformative image features rather than forcing equal representation. If config_039 exceeds 0.653, image adds value and we should explore fusion strategies; if it falls below, image is detrimental and we should focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinement. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves the single largest open design question (multimodal vs. unimodal) while building on the strongest validated RNA settings."
}

